# Neuron web app — local configuration.
#
# Copy this file to `.env.local` beside it. `.env.local` is gitignored; this
# file IS committed.
#
# The address of the API, as the browser will call it: a scheme, a host and a
# port, with no path and no trailing slash. REQUIRED. There is no default, and
# `pnpm dev:web` and `pnpm build:web` both stop with a message when it is
# missing.
#
# The value below is where `pnpm dev` serves the API, so it is correct for
# local development as it stands.
#
# The NEXT_PUBLIC_ prefix is what lets the browser have this value. It also
# means the value is public: it is written into the JavaScript every visitor
# downloads, so nothing secret may ever carry that prefix.
#
# The value is fixed when the app is built. Changing it afterwards needs a
# new build, or a restart of `pnpm dev:web`.
#
# The API has the other half of this pairing: its WEB_ORIGIN must name the
# address this web app is served from. See
# docs/decisions/ADR-018-browser-credential-and-cors.md.
NEXT_PUBLIC_API_URL=http://localhost:3000
